PSBBT7,1,Fill-in-the-blank(s),Numeric,"<p>Han found a way&nbsp;to compute complicated expressions more easily. Since&nbsp;<span><span><span><span>2&nbsp;</span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&sdot;&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span>5</span><span>=</span><span>10</span></span></span></span>, he looks for pairings of 2s and 5s that he knows equal 10. For example,</p>
<p><span><span><span><span><span>3&nbsp;&middot; </span><span><span>2</span><sup><span>4</span></sup></span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;&middot; </span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span><span>5</span><sup><span>5</span></sup><span>&nbsp;</span></span><span>=&nbsp;</span><span>3&nbsp;&middot; </span><span><span>2</span><sup><span>4</span></sup></span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;&middot; </span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span><span>5</span><sup><span>4</span></sup></span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;&middot; </span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span>5&nbsp;</span><span>=&nbsp;</span><span>(</span><span>3&nbsp;&middot; </span><span>5</span><span>)&nbsp;&middot; </span><span>(</span><span>2&nbsp;&middot; </span><span>5</span><span><span>)</span><sup><span>4</span></sup><span>&nbsp;</span></span><span>=&nbsp;</span><span>15&nbsp;&middot; </span><span><span>10</span><sup><span>4</span></sup><span>&nbsp;</span></span><span>=&nbsp;</span><span>150</span><span>,</span><span></span><span>000.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Use Han's technique&nbsp;to compute the following:</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span><span><span>2</span><sup><span>4</span></sup></span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;&middot; </span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span>5&nbsp;&middot; </span><span>(</span><span>3&nbsp;&middot; </span><span>5</span><span><span>)</span><sup><span>3</span></sup></span></span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><ast-r type=""text"" marker=""1""></ast-r></p>",270000,270000,,,7635
PSBBT7,2,Fill-in-the-blank(s),Numeric,"<p>Han found a way&nbsp;to compute complicated expressions more easily. Since&nbsp;<span><span><span><span>2&nbsp;</span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&sdot;&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span>5</span><span>=</span><span>10</span></span></span></span>, he looks for pairings of 2s and 5s that he knows equal 10. For example,</p>
<p><span><span><span><span><span>3&nbsp;&middot; </span><span><span>2</span><sup><span>4</span></sup></span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;&middot; </span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span><span>5</span><sup><span>5</span></sup><span>&nbsp;</span></span><span>=&nbsp;</span><span>3&nbsp;&middot; </span><span><span>2</span><sup><span>4</span></sup></span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;&middot; </span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span><span>5</span><sup><span>4</span></sup></span><span><span><span><span><span><span><span>&nbsp;&middot; </span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span>5&nbsp;</span><span>=&nbsp;</span><span>(</span><span>3&nbsp;&middot; </span><span>5</span><span>)&nbsp;&middot; </span><span>(</span><span>2&nbsp;&middot; </span><span>5</span><span><span>)</span><sup><span>4</span></sup><span>&nbsp;</span></span><span>=&nbsp;</span><span>15&nbsp;&middot; </span><span><span>10</span><sup><span>4</span></sup><span>&nbsp;</span></span><span>=&nbsp;</span><span>150</span><span>,</span><span></span><span>000.</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Use Han's technique&nbsp;to compute the following:</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
