PSBBFAS,1,Fill-in-the-blank(s),Numeric,"<p>Find a four-digit number using only the digits 0, 1, 2, or 3 where:</p>
<ul>
<li>the first digit tells you how many zeros are in the number,<br><br></li>
<li>the second digit tells you how many ones are in the number,<br><br></li>
<li>the third digit tells you how many twos are in the number, and<br><br></li>
<li>the fourth digit tells you how many threes are in the number.</li>
</ul>
<p>The number 2,100 is close, but doesn&rsquo;t quite work. The first digit is 2, and there are 2 zeros. The second digit is 1, and there is 1 one. The fourth digit is 0, and there are no threes. But the third digit, which is supposed to count the number of 2&rsquo;s, is zero.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><ast-r type=""text"" marker=""1""></ast-r></p>","2020, 1210","2020, 1210",,,198955
