PSBB5M6,1,Fill-in-the-blank(s),Numeric,"<p>To make Sierpinski's triangle,</p>
<ul>
<li>Start with an equilateral triangle. This is step 1.</li>
<li>Connect the midpoints of every side, and remove the middle triangle, leaving three&nbsp;smaller triangles. This is step 2.</li>
<li>Do the same to each of the remaining triangles. This is step 3.</li>
<li>Keep repeating this process.</li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img src=""//resources.assistments.org/fetch/C/b803ee8a-6720-406a-9ee0-a09cb65de463.jpeg"" width=""857"" height=""240""></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>What percentage of the area of the original triangle is left after step 2?</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><ast-r type=""text"" marker=""1""></ast-r>%</p>",75,75,,,317639
