PSBT2V,3,Fill-in-the-blank(s),Numeric,"<p>A car is traveling on a small highway and is either going 55 miles per hour or 35 miles per hour, depending on the speed limits, until it reaches its destination 200 miles away. Letting <math xmlns=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML""><mi>x</mi></math> represent the amount of time in hours that the car is going 55 miles per hour, and&nbsp;<math xmlns=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML""><mi>y</mi></math> being the time in hours that the car is going 35 miles per hour, an equation describing the relationship is:&nbsp;<math xmlns=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML""><mn>55</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>35</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn></math>.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>If the car spends no time going 35 miles per hour, how long would the trip take?&nbsp;</p>
