PSBB6QU,1,Fill-in-the-blank(s),Numeric,"<p>Clare made&nbsp;$160 babysitting last summer. She put the money in a savings account that pays 3% interest per year. If Clare doesn&rsquo;t touch the money in her account, she can find the amount she&rsquo;ll have the next year by multiplying her current amount by 1.03.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
