PRABEEXH,1,Fill-in-the-blank(s),Algebraic Expression,"<p>The point where the graphs of two equations intersect has&nbsp;y-coordinate 2. One equation is&nbsp;<math xmlns=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML""><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn></math>. Find the other equation if its graph has a slope of 1.</p>
