<p>Which of these equations represent the relationship between&nbsp;<em>c&nbsp;</em>and&nbsp;<em>f</em>?</p>",,,"<p><math xmlns=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML""><mi>c</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>f</mi></math></p> || <p><math xmlns=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML""><mi>c</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mi>f</mi></math></p> || <p><math xmlns=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML""><mi>c</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mi>f</mi></math></p> || <p><math xmlns=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML""><mi>c</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>f</mi></math></p>","<p><math xmlns=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML""><mi>c</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mi>f</mi></math></p>",97850
PRABEAY2,1,Multiple Choice (select all),Check All That Apply,"<p>Here is an equation that represents a function: <math xmlns=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML""><mn>72</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math>.</p>
