<td style=""width: 87.9829px; text-align: center; height: 21.2822px;""><strong>right-handed</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr style=""height: 34px;"">
<td style=""width: 87.964px; text-align: center; height: 34px;""><strong>7th grade</strong></td>
<td style=""width: 87.964px; text-align: center; height: 34px;"">11</td>
<td style=""width: 87.9829px; text-align: center; height: 34px;"">72</td>
</tr>
<tr style=""height: 34px;"">
<td style=""width: 87.964px; text-align: center; height: 34px;""><strong>8th grade</strong></td>
<td style=""width: 87.964px; text-align: center; height: 34px;"">24</td>
<td style=""width: 87.9829px; text-align: center; height: 34px;"">&nbsp;</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
<td style=""width: 400.672px;""><img src=""/images/assistments/523238.jpg"" alt=""Bar graph."" width=""320"" height=""229""></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Noah found there was&nbsp;<em>no evidence</em> of an association between grade level and handedness. Which of these could be the number of right-handed 8th graders?</p>",,157,33 || 85 || 107 || 157,157,636346
