<div>
<ul>
<li>Andre says he can use long division to divide&nbsp;17&nbsp;by&nbsp;20&nbsp;to get the decimal.</li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>Jada says she can write an equivalent fraction with a denominator of&nbsp;100&nbsp;by multiplying by&nbsp;<math xmlns=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML""><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>, then writing&nbsp;the number of hundredths as a decimal.</li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Do both of these strategies work?</p>
</div>",,,yes || no,yes,353991
