PSBQGS,1,Multiple Choice (select 1),Multiple Choice,"<p>A pollster attends a rally and surveys many of the participants about whether they associate with political Party A or political Party B and whether they are for or against Proposition 3.14 going up for vote soon. The results are sorted into the table shown.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<table style=""height: 73px;"" border=""1"" width=""266"">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td style=""width: 97.5729px; text-align: center;"">&nbsp;</td>
<td style=""width: 52.0833px; text-align: center;""><strong>for</strong></td>
<td style=""width: 97.0104px; text-align: center;""><strong>against</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=""width: 97.5729px; text-align: center;""><strong>party A</strong></td>
<td style=""width: 52.0833px; text-align: center;"">832</td>
<td style=""width: 97.0104px; text-align: center;"">165</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=""width: 97.5729px; text-align: center;""><strong>party B</strong></td>
<td style=""width: 52.0833px; text-align: center;"">80</td>
<td style=""width: 97.0104px; text-align: center;"">160</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<ul>
<li>A news station reports these results by saying, &ldquo;A poll shows that about the same number of people from both parties are voting against Proposition 3.14.&rdquo;</li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
