PSBCHZC,1,Multiple Choice (select all),Check All That Apply,"<p>Andre sometimes mows lawns on the weekend to make extra money. Two weeks ago, he mowed a neighbor&rsquo;s lawn for&nbsp;<math xmlns=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML""><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> hour and earned $10. Last week, he mowed his uncle&rsquo;s lawn for&nbsp;<math xmlns=""http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML""><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> hours and earned&nbsp;$30. This week, he mowed the&nbsp;lawn of a community center&nbsp;for 2 hours and earned&nbsp;$30.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Which jobs paid better than others?&nbsp;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>",,,<p>Neighbor's Lawn</p> || <p>Uncle's Lawn</p> || <p>Community Center</p>,<p>Neighbor's Lawn</p> || <p>Uncle's Lawn</p>,389028
PSBBY9D,1,Multiple Choice (select 1),Multiple Choice,"<p>The equation&nbsp;<span><span><span><span>a&nbsp;</span><span>+&nbsp;</span><span>b&nbsp;</span><span>=&nbsp;</span><span>c</span></span></span></span>&nbsp;could be true or false.</p>
