PSBJF8,1,Multiple Choice (select 1),Multiple Choice,"<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><img src=""/images/assistments/333109.jpg"" width=""365"" height=""121"">&nbsp;</p>
<p>Diego and Jada were asked &ldquo;How many rhombuses are in a trapezoid?&rdquo;</p>
<ul>
<li>Diego says, &ldquo;<img src=""/pluginwiris_engine/app/showimage?formula=b37f1195c1789520bde304bcb5356a78"" data-mathml=""&laquo;math xmlns=&uml;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&uml;&raquo;&laquo;mn&raquo;1&laquo;/mn&raquo;&laquo;mfrac&raquo;&laquo;mn&raquo;1&laquo;/mn&raquo;&laquo;mn&raquo;3&laquo;/mn&raquo;&laquo;/mfrac&raquo;&laquo;/math&raquo;"">. If I put 1 rhombus on a trapezoid, the leftover shape is a triangle, which is <img src=""/pluginwiris_engine/app/showimage?formula=9946ec629e826fbb8a5653043a3464db"" data-mathml=""&laquo;math xmlns=&uml;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&uml;&raquo;&laquo;mfrac&raquo;&laquo;mn&raquo;1&laquo;/mn&raquo;&laquo;mn&raquo;3&laquo;/mn&raquo;&laquo;/mfrac&raquo;&laquo;/math&raquo;"">&nbsp;of the trapezoid.&rdquo;&nbsp;</li>
<li>Jada says, &ldquo;I think it&rsquo;s <img src=""/pluginwiris_engine/app/showimage?formula=3a9f5ca93dacb9adfae17e79bd3901b9"" data-mathml=""&laquo;math xmlns=&uml;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&uml;&raquo;&laquo;mn&raquo;1&laquo;/mn&raquo;&laquo;mfrac&raquo;&laquo;mn&raquo;1&laquo;/mn&raquo;&laquo;mn&raquo;2&laquo;/mn&raquo;&laquo;/mfrac&raquo;&laquo;/math&raquo;"">. Since we want to find out &lsquo;how many rhombuses,&rsquo; we should compare the leftover triangle to a rhombus. A triangle is <img src=""/pluginwiris_engine/app/showimage?formula=3bdddc87db3186caf445c7636a0cdcbc"" data-mathml=""&laquo;math xmlns=&uml;http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML&uml;&raquo;&laquo;mfrac&raquo;&laquo;mn&raquo;1&laquo;/mn&raquo;&laquo;mn&raquo;2&laquo;/mn&raquo;&laquo;/mfrac&raquo;&laquo;/math&raquo;"">&nbsp;of a rhombus.&rdquo;&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Do you agree with either of them?</p>",,,I agree with Diego || I agree with Jada || I agree with neither || I agree with both,I agree with Jada,44207
