PSBUVN,1,Multiple Choice (select 1),Multiple Choice,"<p>Tyler and Han are discussing the question, ""Which sixth-grade student lives the farthest from school?""</p>
<ul>
<li>Tyler says, &ldquo;I don&rsquo;t think the question is a statistical question. There is only one person who lives the farthest from school, so there would not be variability in the data we collect.&rdquo;</li>
<li>Han says: &ldquo;I think it is a statistical question. To answer the question, we wouldn&rsquo;t actually be asking everyone, 'Which student lives the farthest from school?' We would have to ask each student how far away from school they live, and we can expect their responses to have variability.&rdquo;</li>
</ul>
<p>Do you agree with either of them?</p>",,,Agree with Tyler || Agree with Han,Agree with Han,94609
