<td style=""width: 80.303px; text-align: center;""><strong>play sports</strong></td>
<td style=""width: 80.303px; text-align: center;""><strong>don't play sports</strong></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=""width: 80.303px; text-align: center;""><strong>7th graders</strong></td>
<td style=""width: 80.303px; text-align: center;"">112</td>
<td style=""width: 80.303px; text-align: center;"">52</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td style=""width: 80.303px; text-align: center;""><strong>8th graders</strong></td>
<td style=""width: 80.303px; text-align: center;"">&nbsp;</td>
<td style=""width: 80.303px; text-align: center;"">84</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
<td style=""width: 454.205px;""><img src=""/images/assistments/523240.jpg"" alt=""Bar chart"" width=""351"" height=""211""></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Jada found there was no evidence of an association between grade level and playing sports. Which of these could be the number of 8th graders who play sports?</p>",,181,248 || 181 || 144 || 69,181,604503
