<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Select&nbsp;<strong>all</strong>&nbsp;the true statements about such cones.</p>",,,"The relationship between radius and volume is linear. || The relationship between radius and volume is not linear. || If the radius of the cone doubles, the volume of the cone doubles. || If the radius of the cone doubles, the volume of the cone is multiplied by 4. || If the radius of the cone is 2 inches, the volume of the cone is about 25 cubic inches.","The relationship between radius and volume is not linear. || If the radius of the cone doubles, the volume of the cone is multiplied by 4. || If the radius of the cone is 2 inches, the volume of the cone is about 25 cubic inches.",297716
